// D1587 — the `i32` an `x as! u8` yields, delivered everywhere. The trapping face of the same
// ruling: `u8` names 0..255 rather than a value type, so `x as! u8` narrows exactly-or-traps
// and the value that comes out is an ordinary `i32` in that range.
//
// The `as!` face is the one a `u8[]` consumer writes (`bytes.push(x as! u8)`), so it has to
// survive every delivery the plain `i32` does — and it is the face the emitter's PEEPHOLE
// could have broken: `trunc(d) as! i32` skips the exactness test because the conversion
// instruction enforces i32's range, and that argument is false at 0..255.
//
// The PROOF adds, so a cell that widened or wrapped prints something other than 201.
//
// Format: scripts/capability-probes/matrix.py, whose docstring is the spec.
// @@PRELUDE@@
function inRange(): f64 { return 200.0 }
function alsoInRange(): f64 { return 12.0 }
// @@VALUE@@
inRange() as! u8
// @@TYPE@@
i32
// @@PROOF@@
print(v + 1)
// @@WANT@@
201
// @@TEST@@
v > 100
// @@HIT@@
print(v + 1)
// @@MISS@@
print(0)
// @@VALUE2@@
alsoInRange() as! u8
// @@TYPE2@@
i32
// @@PROOF2@@
print(v + 1)
// @@WANT2@@
13
